      },
      "worked": "There are $5!$ red configurations: choose a distinct column for the red counter in each row.\n\nFix one red configuration. There are $5!$ blue configurations before excluding coincidences. For any specified $k$ rows, fixing the blue counters at the red positions leaves $(5-k)!$ configurations. There are $\\binom{5}{k}$ ways to choose these rows.\n\nLet $B$ be the number of permissible blue configurations for this fixed red configuration. By inclusion–exclusion,\n$$\\begin{align*}B&=5!-\\binom51 4!+\\binom52 3!-\\binom53 2!+\\binom54 1!-\\binom55 0!\\\\B&=120-120+60-20+5-1\\\\B&=44.\\end{align*}$$\nBy the multiplication principle, the total number $N$ is\n$$\\begin{align*}N&=5!\\times44\\\\N&=5280.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
